(5574947, 805352, 54645, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> I didn''t like the silly title, but there was no better photo in this challenge. I gave this an 8. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Don! <br/> <br/>About the title...I decided to quote Abby. After I handed her Sophia,she looked up at me and said "What? No diaper?". That''s why she has that concerned and questioning expression. The subsequent pictures were full of happy smiles, but that expression is priceless (at least to her Dad!) as is the sacked out position of the infant.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-07-15 11:55:05.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: I didn''t like the silly title, but there was no better photo in this challenge. I gave this an 8.   Thanks Don!  About the title...I decided to quote Abby. After I handed her Sophia,she looked up at me and said "What? No diaper?". That''s why she has that concerned and questioning expression. The subsequent pictures were full of happy smiles, but that expression is priceless (at least to her Dad!) as is the sacked out position of the infant.', '2009-07-15 12:52:49.000000', '2009-07-15 12:55:05.000000', 0),
